.nh
.TH "PB-CONFIG-ASSIGN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-assign - Assign a config repository to a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config assign <repository> <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Assign a config repository to a machine

.PP
Bind a repository to the named enrolled machine and choose pull/push behavior with --mode and repository options. Automatic updates are explicit; the confirmation code acknowledges that selected content is plaintext in private Git history.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--automatic-updates\fP[=false]
	apply later reviewed-scope updates automatically

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code for plaintext Git storage

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for assign

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--mode\fP="pull-only"
	sync mode: pull-only, push-only, or bidirectional

.PP
\fB--pull-repository\fP=""
	repository used for pulls (defaults to positional repository)

.PP
\fB--push-repository\fP=""
	repository used for pushes (defaults to positional repository)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP
